course: dictionary
lesson: 10255
title: The tone of a voice
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Tone is the way something sounds, or the feeling behind the words. The same words can sound friendly or rude depending on the tone. «Please sit down», said kindly, is an invitation. Said through clenched teeth, it is an order.
explain: A writer also has a tone: the mood of a story or poem, such as happy, sad, spooky or serious. Look at the words the writer picks, because they leave clues. Short, sharp words often make a story feel tense.
explain: Tone can also mean a single musical note or a beep, like a phone's dial tone. In art, a tone is a lighter or darker shade of a colour. And «tone down» means to make something less strong: if you are cross, tone down your reply so it sounds gentler.
fact: Tone is the way something sounds, or the feeling behind the words.
fact: The tone of a piece of writing is its mood or feeling, such as happy, sad, spooky or serious.
fact: «Tone of voice» matters: the same words can be polite or rude.
fact: A tone is also a single musical sound, or a beep such as a phone's dial tone.
fact: «To tone down» something means to make it less strong. «Tone up» muscles means to make them firmer with exercise.
exercise: «The tone of a voice — loud, quiet, shaky or flat — can show how someone feels.» What can the tone of a voice show? | *How someone feels | How tall they are | How many books they have read | The colour of their coat
exercise: Mia says «Thanks for the present», but her tone is flat and she rolls her eyes. What does the tone tell you? | She is shouting with joy | *She may not really mean it | She has lost her voice | She is singing a song
exercise: Which phrase means to make something less strong? | Tone of voice | *Tone down | Tone up the sky | Dial tone
test: In a story where the wind howls and a door creaks slowly open, what is the tone? | Happy | Sleepy | *Spooky | Silly
test: In art, what is a tone? | *A shade of a colour, lighter or darker | A kind of cake | A type of shoe | A loud shout
exam: «To spot sarcasm, check whether the words fit the situation and the tone.» What should you check to spot sarcasm? | Whether the page is white | How many letters are in the title | The length of the words | *Whether the words fit the situation and the tone
